        "evidence": {
          "date": "Mon, Nov 16",
          "time": "3:00pm",
          "venue": "East Hall",
          "admission": "Free",
          "description": "Traditionally, foliations in positive characteristic have been studied using subsets of the module of derivations. Unfortunately, the theory does not seem to behave well geometrically, for instance Bernasconi showed that they fail many MMP statements. In this talk, I will show how to use purely inseparable Galois theory to develop a new notion of foliation in positive characteristic that seems to have much better behaviour. This is joint work with Carvajal-Rojas, Ciprietti, and FakhriVaighan.",
          "end": "4:00pm"
        }
      },
